   "AreaReportContent_Text1": "A storyteller's script based on historical events, recounting the history of the Jinzhou region in Huanglong.\n \n ...",
   "AreaReportContent_Text10": "What time is it now? Six? It must be six in the morning. The next surgery should start soon. We're gathered in a meeting room on one of the higher floors, but this isn't the time to be picky. A team this size needs at least three Peregrine Falcon ornithopters for evacuation.\n \n...We're down to just 13 doses of atropine. The heat is rising, and keeping the wounded cool is becoming impossible.\n \nWhere are the reinforcements? Where is the air force? HQ! This is a call for immediate support! Coordinates are back to the Tethys System—we need reinforcements!\n \n...At least... evacuate the elders and children...\n \nIt's getting hotter and hotter, and Brandon's team hasn't returned... Calling for reinforcements...\n...\nDon't lose... hope...",
   "AreaReportContent_Text100": "Twistscales\n \nListen. A low whistle, carried on the scrape of friction, approaches from afar. That sphere, draped in hardened scales, bounds and weaves between steep cliff faces.\n\nThis is the Twistscale, one of the most peculiar creatures inhabiting these wilds. Each morning as the mist disperses, it is driven by an ancient and powerful instinct—to collect.\n\nBeneath its heavy scales lies an extraordinarily keen nervous system. As it rolls and crawls, these hidden senses precisely map the size of nearby minerals, the position of fallen fruit, the lie of branches upon the ground. Once it locks onto a target, powerful muscles draw the scales tight, gripping nature's gifts firm and fast. Tireless, the Twistscale rolls without rest until nightfall, as if intent on curling away the entire mountainside.\n\nBut in the harsh wilds, greed exacts a heavy toll.\n\nAs the \"spoils\" wedged between its scales accumulate, the Twistscale can no longer maintain its compact, nimble form. To bear the weight, it must unfurl its limbs. At this moment, the once-swift cliff-runner moves like an aged tortoise through mud, each step laborious, each breath heavy, stopping often, pressing on.\n\nBut the wilds are fraught with danger. Predators lurk in unseen corners, and once a threat is perceived, it curls into a ball at once. With a sharp clatter, its scales snap shut in fright—and the treasures nestled between the seams slip free. A day's labor scatters across the ground.\n\nTypically, the Twistscale remains curled for about ten minutes, then begins to roll slowly until it confirms the danger has passed. Only then does it relax. After a moment's rest, it coils once more and begins gathering its scattered spoils.\n\nShould this occur as the sun descends into the western sky, the Twistscale returns to the safe burrow constructed from Jade Hexahedron, Floral Crest Jade, and tree branches. There, and only there, does it flip onto its belly and spend the night in its most comfortable posture.",
-  "AreaReportContent_Text101": "",
-  "AreaReportContent_Text102": "",
+  "AreaReportContent_Text101": "Stay tuned",
+  "AreaReportContent_Text102": "Stay tuned",
   "AreaReportContent_Text11": "...We have conducted extensive research on Hoochief behaviors, compiled in this book. Below are excerpts from our observations, so that our readers can compare behavioral changes in Hoochiefs before and after exposure to toxic spores, as well as before and after improvements in the biological environment of the Dim Forest.\n \nHoochiefs Not Exposed to Toxic Spores:\nHoochiefs are a patriarchal, pack-oriented species with a strong territorial instinct. The core members of the pack lead them to collaborate in teams to repel any intruders from their domain.\n\nUninfected Hoochiefs can communicate with each other and use simple tools made of stones and sticks.",
   "AreaReportContent_Text12": "Hoochiefs Exposed to Toxic Spores:\nInfected Hoochiefs develop grey eyes and exhibit anxious, erratic behaviors as the toxic spores infiltrate their bodies, resulting in frequent coughing and vomiting. They may also compulsively scratch and tear at their own backs. In the final stage of infection, each violent cough releases a mist of spores, making them highly contagious sources of infection.\n\nInfected Hoochiefs attack any nearby creatures indiscriminately.\n \nHoochiefs After Environmental Improvements in the Dim Forest:\nFollowing improvements to the Dim Forest's biological environment, new cases of Hoochief infections from toxic spores have dropped significantly. Thanks to the intervention of antibodies developed by the Dim Forest exploration team, infections among Hoochiefs have gradually disappeared, ultimately dispelling the darkness that once shrouded the Dim Forest.",
   "AreaReportContent_Text13": "The Exiles are not a criminal organization with a unified leadership. Rather, the term refers to individuals who reject the control of local authorities and roam the wilds. They come from all walks of life and form a diverse, mixed group. While not inherently malicious, they have few qualms about committing illegal acts such as theft or robbery.\n \nTo survive in the harsh, unsheltered wilderness, they make use of scavenged materials and repurpose technology. Each Exile is typically armed with a Tacetite Weapon, obtained through illegal means, to defend against the threat of TDs or rival Exile gangs.\n \nJinzhou's stance toward the Exiles is primarily preventative, with security forces deployed in areas frequented by them. For those Exiles without significant offenses, the authorities generally adopt a more lenient approach and sometimes try to persuade them to submit under certain conditions. However, for Exiles who are recalcitrant and pose a security risk, the authorities are quick to eliminate them without hesitation.\n \nGiven the Exiles' long history, it is now difficult to trace when the first true Exile emerged.\n \nThere are numerous reasons why someone might choose to join the Exiles in the wilderness: a thief seeking to escape the Patrollers, a deserter too ashamed to face their comrades, or a Resonator who believes they can protect themselves but refuses to adhere to local laws. To become an Exile, one must first defeat another Exile—whether by taking their life, stealing their Ring, or seizing it by force, a symbol of severance from mainstream society. That is how an Exile earns recognition from their peers.",
@@ -7711,8 +7711,8 @@
